  "description": "Dynamic braking reverses the role of the traction motors during deceleration: the motors act as generators, converting the train's kinetic energy into electrical energy, which is dissipated as heat in a resistor grid (rheostatic) or returned to the line (regenerative, on electric networks). Reduces brake shoe wear and prevents thermal fade on long downgrades.",
